{"id":"resp_80fd1cc351586a2c","created_at":1795618074,"incomplete_details":null,"instructions":null,"metadata":null,"model":"gpt-oss-120b","object":"response","output":[{"id":"rs_bedbfdaa947c826d","summary":[],"type":"reasoning","content":[{"text":"The task: Revise previous_candidate (the SHACL shape) to fix errors found in current_findings, while preserving everything else. The main errors: \"Unknown namespace prefix : nltl\" in the SPARQL SELECT blocks; prefix declarations missing inside the SPARQL queries. The hint says to add PREFIX declaration for nltl namespace at the beginning of each SPARQL SELECT block or ensure the SHACL engine inherits document-level prefixes for SPARQL constraints. In the shape, the document-level prefixes are already declared at top:\n\n@prefix nltl: <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#> .\n\nThe issue likely is that pySHACL doesn't propagate these prefixes into SPARQL constraints; each SPARQL query must include its own PREFIX declarations.\n\nThus we need to modify each sh:select block to prepend PREFIX nltl: <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#> and maybe also PREFIX qudt: <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/> and any other prefixes used: qudt: is used with unit declarations; they are also defined at top. But the error only mentions nltl, so adding PREFIX nltl may be enough.\n\nThe query also uses qudt:numericValue and qudt:unit. Since qudt is declared globally, but to be safe can also add PREFIX qudt: <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/> (but qudt's unit prefix is maybe full URL; actual prefix declaration is \"@prefix qudt: <http://www.qudt.org/vocab/unit#> .\". So inside SPARQL we need \"PREFIX qudt: <http://www.qudt.org/vocab/unit#>\" as well. However they used qudt:numericValue, qudt:unit but the IRI for QUDT unit is \"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit\" but the Prefix is correct: \"@prefix qudt: <http://www.qudt.org/vocab/unit#> .\". The global prefix should work or may need to be added.\n\nThe easiest: add \"PREFIX nltl: <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#>\" at start of each SELECT query (inside the string). Possibly add \"PREFIX qudt: <http://www.qudt.org/vocab/unit#>\" as well for completeness.\n\nThe constraints have four sh:select blocks (select[0] through select[3]). Need to modify each.\n\nAlso ensure the shape targetClass remains same.\n\nMake sure the shape has proper formatting.\n\nDo not delete any constraints.\n\nThus we produce revised SHACL code with PREFIX declarations inside each SPARQL.\n\nLet's construct final shape.\n\nWe'll copy earlier shape and for each sh:select string, embed:\n\nPREFIX nltl: <https://w0id.org/nltl/vocab#> Actually correct: \"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#\". Ensure matches.\n\nAlso maybe need to include PREFIX qudt: <http://www.qudt.org/vocab/unit#>.\n\nWe'll add both.\n\nThe queries:\n\nSELECT $this ( ?operDraughtVal AS ?value )\nWHERE {\n   ...\n\nNow we will prepend:\n\nPREFIX nltl: <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#>\nPREFIX qudt: <http://www.qudt.org/vocab/unit#>\n\nInside the query string.\n\nDo the same for all four.\n\nNow output as required: <BEGIN_SHACL> ... <END_SHACL>.\n\nWe must ensure the shape includes proper indentation and triple quotes.\n\nWill produce final answer.\n\n","type":"reasoning_text"}],"encrypted_content":null,"status":null},{"id":"msg_9dc5fc38e0978a85","content":[{"annotations":[],"text":"<BEGIN_SHACL>\n@prefix sh: <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .\n@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .\n@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .\n@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .\n@prefix qudt: <http://www.qudt.org/vocab/unit#> .\n@prefix nltl: <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#> .\n\n# Shape targeting all ships (benchmark entities)\nnltl:ShipIceNavigationShape\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\n    sh:targetClass nltl:ship ;\n    sh:label \"Ship – Ice navigation and salinity constraints (TRF‑015 clause 2.2)\" ;\n    sh:description \"\"\"Implements the requirement:\n    – When the ship is navigating in ice, the operating draught must not exceed the Upper Ice Waterline (UIWL).\n    – The operating trim must not exceed the maximum permitted ice trim.\n    – The salinity of the sea water along the intended route must be taken into account when loading the ship.\n    \"\"\" ;\n    \n    # -------------------------------------------------\n    # 1. Draught shall not exceed UIWL when navigating in ice\n    # -------------------------------------------------\n    sh:sparql [\n        a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;\n        sh:message \"When navigating in ice the operating draught exceeds the Upper Ice Waterline draught.\" ;\n        sh:select \"\"\"\n            PREFIX nltl: <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#>\n            PREFIX qudt: <http://www.qudt.org/vocab/unit#>\n            SELECT $this ( ?operDraughtVal AS ?value )\n            WHERE {\n                $this nltl:navigatingInIce true .\n                $this nltl:operatingDraught ?operDraught .\n                $this nltl:upperIceWaterlineDraught ?uiwl .\n                \n                ?operDraught qudt:numericValue ?operDraughtVal .\n                ?operDraught qudt:unit <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/M> .\n                \n                ?uiwl qudt:numericValue ?uiwlVal .\n                ?uiwl qudt:unit <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/M> .\n                \n                FILTER ( ?operDraughtVal > ?uiwlVal )\n            }\n        \"\"\" ;\n    ] ;\n    \n    # -------------------------------------------------\n    # 2. Trim shall not exceed the maximum permitted ice trim when navigating in ice\n    # -------------------------------------------------\n    sh:sparql [\n        a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;\n        sh:message \"When navigating in ice the operating trim exceeds the maximum permitted ice trim.\" ;\n        sh:select \"\"\"\n            PREFIX nltl: <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#>\n            PREFIX qudt: <http://www.qudt.org/vocab/unit#>\n            SELECT $this ( ?operTrimVal AS ?value )\n            WHERE {\n                $this nltl:navigatingInIce true .\n                $this nltl:operatingTrim ?operTrim .\n                $this nltl:maximumPermittedIceTrim ?maxTrim .\n                \n                ?operTrim qudt:numericValue ?operTrimVal .\n                ?operTrim qudt:unit <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/M> .\n                \n                ?maxTrim qudt:numericValue ?maxTrimVal .\n                ?maxTrim qudt:unit <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/M> .\n                \n                FILTER ( ?operTrimVal > ?maxTrimVal )\n            }\n        \"\"\" ;\n    ] ;\n    \n    # -------------------------------------------------\n    # 3. Salinity values must be present when navigating in ice\n    # -------------------------------------------------\n    # 3a – intended route sea‑water salinity\n    sh:sparql [\n        a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;\n        sh:message \"When navigating in ice the intended route sea‑water salinity is missing or has an invalid unit.\" ;\n        sh:select \"\"\"\n            PREFIX nltl: <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#>\n            PREFIX qudt: <http://www.qudt.org/vocab/unit#>\n            SELECT $this\n            WHERE {\n                $this nltl:navigatingInIce true .\n                FILTER NOT EXISTS {\n                    $this nltl:intendedRouteSeaWaterSalinity ?salinity .\n                    ?salinity qudt:numericValue ?val .\n                    ?salinity qudt:unit <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#gramPerKilogramSalinityUnit> .\n                }\n            }\n        \"\"\" ;\n    ] ;\n    \n    # 3b – loading‑calculation sea‑water salinity\n    sh:sparql [\n        a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;\n        sh:message \"When navigating in ice the loading‑calculation sea‑water salinity is missing or has an invalid unit.\" ;\n        sh:select \"\"\"\n            PREFIX nltl: <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#>\n            PREFIX qudt: <http://www.qudt.org/vocab/unit#>\n            SELECT $this\n            WHERE {\n                $this nltl:navigatingInIce true .\n                FILTER NOT EXISTS {\n                    $this nltl:loadingCalculationSeaWaterSalinity ?salCalc .\n                    ?salCalc qudt:numericValue ?val .\n                    ?salCalc qudt:unit <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#gramPerKilogramSalinityUnit> .\n                }\n            }\n        \"\"\" ;\n    ] .\n<END_SHACL>","type":"output_text","logprobs":null}],"role":"assistant","status":"completed","type":"message","phase":null}],"parallel_tool_calls":true,"temperature":1.0,"tool_choice":"none","tools":[],"top_p":1.0,"background":false,"max_output_tokens":16000,"max_tool_calls":null,"previous_response_id":null,"prompt":null,"prompt_cache_options":null,"prompt_cache_key":null,"prompt_cache_retention":null,"reasoning":null,"safety_identifier":null,"service_tier":"auto","status":"completed","text":null,"top_logprobs":null,"truncation":"disabled","usage":{"input_tokens":92063,"input_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":320,"cache_write_tokens":91728,"input_tokens_per_turn":[92063],"cached_tokens_per_turn":[320]},"output_tokens":1962,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":737,"tool_output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_per_turn":[1962],"tool_output_tokens_per_turn":[0]},"total_tokens":94025},"user":null,"presence_penalty":0.0,"frequency_penalty":0.0,"kv_transfer_params":null,"ec_transfer_params":null,"input_messages":null,"output_messages":null}